1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,560
Why does your foot fall asleep?

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:02,760
It isn't asleep.

3
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:05,750
A nerve in your leg is being squashed.

4
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:07,390
When you sit on your foot or cross

5
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:09,690
your legs, you press on that nerve, and

6
00:00:09,690 --> 00:00:11,740
on the tiny blood vessels that feed it.

7
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,020
A squashed nerve can't pass messages.

8
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:16,320
Your brain stops hearing from your foot,

9
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,570
so it goes numb.

10
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:18,770
Then you stand up.

11
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:21,030
The pressure lifts, and the nerve restarts

12
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:23,420
all at once, firing messy signals.

13
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,860
And that buzzing static...

14
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:26,440
is pins and needles.

15
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,200
Your nerve, waking up.
